---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const SITE = 'https://dogtur.com';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Dogtur"
  description="Dogtur privacy policy: what data we collect (almost none) and how affiliate links work."
  canonical={`${SITE}/privacy-policy/`}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: September 2026.</em></p>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      Dogtur is a static website. We don't run user accounts, comments, or
      newsletters (yet). We don't ask for your name, email, or dog's details to
      read the site.
    </p>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We don't run first-party analytics on this site — no tracking scripts,
      no cookies set by us. Our host (Cloudflare) processes standard,
      anonymized web logs to serve the pages. If we add a privacy-friendly,
      cookieless analytics tool in the future, we'll document it here; if a
      cookie-based tool is ever added, this policy and the site will be
      updated first.
    </p>
    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      Clicking an affiliate link takes you to a retailer's site, which sets its
      own cookies and applies its own privacy policy. We don't see or store
      what you buy. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you email us, we keep your message only long enough to respond.
      Privacy questions: use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
